(text "USB-C 5V input: source qualification, voltage/current protection, hardware suspend cutoff" (at 20.32 17.78 0) (effects (font (size 2 2)) (justify left top)) (uuid be1f3873-7942-4721-889b-dcdaa3dd1dbf))
(text "U23 NVM: one 5V / 1.5A sink PDO; program and read back before shipment. No higher-voltage load mode.\nSOURCE_ALLOWED requires advertised Type-C >=1.5A OR a valid 5V PD contract >=1.5A; default OFF.\nUSB_SUSPEND_EXEMPT requires current, fresh source evidence, not merely a requested RDO flag.\nU26: (USB_AWAKE OR USB_SUSPEND_EXEMPT) AND SOURCE_ALLOWED. U27 translates to protected 5V.\nSN6505 EN requires 0.7 x VCC: a direct 3.3V enable is not sufficient at 5V. R79 remains the output pull-down.\nPD alert, USB_AWAKE and RTC alarm wake U24 from STOP; unprogrammed MCU leaves the scoring supply OFF.\nThe CP2102N and source controller enumerate/qualify independently of the isolated processors.\nU25 is automatic-retry current limit, nominal 1.21A; 10nF dVdt gives approximately 25ms 5V ramp.\nUVLO nominal 4.04V rising / 3.69V falling. OVLO nominal 5.38V rising / 4.91V falling.\nReview threshold tolerance and measured overshoot, inrush, radio load and complete USB-suspend current before release.\nUSB_GND is the laptop-side ground. Never join it to isolated scoring GND or the piste.\nJ7 is an unpopulated pogo-pad service target, not an extra fitted header." (at 20.32 310 0) (effects (font (size 1.2 1.2)) (justify left top)) (uuid a857f1d2-2b8a-4219-96d2-98bb892bfb58))
(no_connect (at 342.9 86.36) (uuid 134342c9-bcd8-4dc1-b302-e4fe5a378a28))
